  "modules": [
    {
      "name": "Benchmark",
      "source": "Src/Benchmark.rux",
      "header": "Measuring how long code takes: running it often enough to time it reliably, and reporting the time per iteration.\nA benchmark runs its own loop over the iteration count it is given, so whatever it sets up before the loop is not\ncounted, and calling it costs nothing per iteration. The count grows from one until a run lasts long enough for the\nclock to measure it well."
    },
    {
      "name": "Expect",
      "source": "Src/Expect.rux",
      "header": "Checks that fail a test with a message saying what was expected and what was found.\nEach check returns `! TestFailure`, so a test passes it on with `?` and stops at the first check that does not hold."
    },
    {
      "name": "Failure",
      "source": "Src/Failure.rux",
      "header": "Why a test did not pass: a failure with its message, or a skip with its reason.\nThe message is kept inline, so a failure can be made and passed on without an allocator and never fails itself; a\nmessage longer than the room is cut short."
    },
    {
      "name": "Runner",
      "source": "Src/Runner.rux",
      "header": "Running a table of tests: choosing them by name, timing each, and reporting.\nThe tests run one after another in this process, so a test that panics or fails an `Assert` ends the run there; a\nfailed check, through `TestFailure`, ends only its own test."
    }
  ],
